{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show the 3D scene rendered properly in Chrome with no blank screen or visual errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 show orbiting and zooming; OrbitControls in the code sets maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.465 (keeping camera above y=0) and maxDistance = 15.5 (inside the 34x34 tablecloth).",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "The scene uses moderate procedural geometry (~40 meshes plus one InstancedMesh and one Points object), two shadow maps (2048 and 1024), and EffectComposer with BokehPass and UnrealBloomPass, which should run at 30+ fps on a typical laptop.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots show an on-screen UI bar at the bottom ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom', 'Macro DoF: ON', 'Hero Angle').",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "In the `animate()` function in the HTML source, only camera reset lerping, `controls.update()`, DoF focus distance, and `composer.render()` run; there is zero environmental motion.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 shows a close-up, slightly elevated angle with the French toast stack centered on the plate, matching the framing of the reference photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 5 clearly show three thick slices of French toast stacked and rotationally offset.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show banana slices tucked between the toast layers, on top, and resting on the plate to the left and front.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show blueberries clustered on top of the stack and scattered around the base of the toast on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the stack resting on a dark round plate set on a grey-brown linen surface, though in Screenshot 5 the cloth stops at a stark black void horizon.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show white powdered sugar specks dusted across the dark plate and lightly on the top toast slice and berries.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the toast slices look like wavy-edged crackers or plastic molds with uniform vertical ridges rather than thick bread slices with a natural rounded loaf crust and soft cut edges.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show round banana discs with a faint brownish three-pointed seed pattern in the center, though several slices have dark metallic-looking bevel rims.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show round blueberries of slightly varying sizes with sculpted 5-pointed star crowns visible on top.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 1, the right corner of the middle toast slice hovers unsupported, and in Screenshot 2 a blueberry near the center-right hangs mid-air underneath the middle slice.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 5 (zoomed out) and Screenshots 1–3, the tablecloth plane ends abruptly in the background revealing a solid black void edge across the top of the frame, and banana slices clip visibly through the toast geometry in Screenshot 2.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the code (`keyLight.position.set(-5.2, 8.4, 5.4)`) and Screenshot 1, the main key light comes from the front-left rather than behind-left, and the syrup rivulets appear dark brown rather than catching bright warm window highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 1, despite `BokehPass` being active (`maxblur: 0.0065`), the back rim of the plate and the horizon edge of the cloth remain nearly sharp rather than softly blurred like the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 1 and 4, several blueberries on top of the toast and the banana slice on the left of the plate lack convincing soft contact shadows grounding them.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "At the very top of Screenshot 1 (and prominently in Screenshot 5), the background above the tablecloth is a completely flat, near-black void (`0x161412`) with zero detail.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1 and 5, the syrup rivulets on the toast crust look like dark, opaque brown worms and the puddles on the plate look like flat reddish-brown shapes without bright specular highlights or amber translucency.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the toast has smooth, plastic-like airbrushed vertex colors with pale yellow centers and uniform brown edges, lacking any porous bread crumb or realistic uneven caramelisation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the blueberries have high-contrast blotchy white/blue noise textures that read like marbled stone rather than a subtle, dusty matte wax bloom.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the banana slices look opaque and chalky white/grey with unnatural dark grey metallic shading around their curved bevel edges rather than moist, slightly translucent fruit.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1 and 5, the plate shows a dark satin/glossy ceramic sheen (though interrupted by a circular artifact ring from the transmission pass), while the cloth looks like a blurry grey noise plane rather than clearly woven linen fabric.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the plate and table surface sitting completely level with no unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "The syrup meshes built in `addCrustSyrupRivulets` are static `TubeGeometry` meshes and are never animated in `animate()`.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "Neither the screenshots nor the HTML source contain any steam or warm haze particle system or shader.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no environmental motion in the scene (`animate()` only updates camera controls and renders).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "All blueberries share the exact same UV-mapped `berryTex` texture, and in Screenshot 1 and 4 adjacent berries on top and at the front show noticeably similar blotchy patterns, though rotated.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 4 show severe clipping: banana slices on top and between layers intersect directly through the toast surfaces, and syrup/banana geometry clips at the base.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the sugar on the plate consists of large, distinct, uniform white dots (`IcosahedronGeometry(0.015)`) that look like coarse salt or styrofoam beads rather than fine powdered sugar.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 looks distinctly like stylized 3D computer graphics—with plastic wavy-edged toast, blotchy berries, clipping bananas, coarse white dots, and a UI bar—and could not pass for the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
